{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-braid-group-n-strand","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:braid-group-n-strand","kind":"remark","title":"$n$-strand braid group, Markov closure, and Hecke quadratic quotient: axiomatic framework generalising the 2-strand $\\mathbf{B}_2$ foundation and 3-strand typed-$\\mathbf{B}_3$ infrastructure","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-markov-axioms-primitive","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms","cites":["references/jones1985","references/kassel1995","references/wenzl1988"],"tags":["lean-infrastructure","braid-group","n-strand","hecke-algebra","markov-closure","scaffolding"],"text":"braid-group-n-strand.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:braid-group-n-strand\"></a><p>To compute the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}_M(K_1 \\sqcup K_2)</code> inter-knot decoupling, the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B_3</code> framework generalises to arbitrary <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>-strand braid groups and Hecke quotients. Results stated for general <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> then specialise to each fixed <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> as higher strand numbers are analysed.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/braid-group-n-strand.md","heading":"Remark","number":"7.3.21","page":"b/rem-braid-group-n-strand","qa":{"counts":{"pass":58,"fail":2,"warn":2,"na":15,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
